  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This recording captures a sold-out performance by the Mountain Goats at the Ecstatic Music Festival on Saturday, March 24, 2012 [1]. Presented by Q2 Music as a live audio webcast, the event featured the band alongside the acclaimed early vocal music ensemble Anonymous 4 [1]. The audio file, transferred by Jimbers, runs for 89 minutes and includes 27 songs [1]. The first thirty minutes consist of a set by Anonymous 4, which the uploader included as a single long audio file at the end of the recording [1]. The Mountain Goats portion begins with “Tribe of the Horned Heart,” the only archived performance of that song [1][2]. Other rare tracks include “Bride” and “In the Shadow of the Western Hills,” each with only three archived performances [2]. The set also features “South Western Vultures” and “Hail Saint Sebastion,” both noted as the only archived performances of their respective songs [1][2]. The band performs “Your Belgian Things” and “Wild Sage,” followed by “Enoch 18 14” [1][2]. The show concludes with a joint set by the Mountain Goats and Anonymous 4, which is the only archived performance of that specific configuration [1][2]. This is the 168th archived show for the performer, following a previous recording from January 31, 2012 [2]. The recording is recommended as the only available capture of this specific concert [1].",
